      "source_example_id": "e-8905",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrals Representing Surface Areas Generated by Functions of X",
      "kp_id": "e-8905"
    },
    "q-126540": {
      "dom_id": "step-q126540",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14131010/assets/68a30adbe260a15c8514ceec2291da4be77af2335f8999d512ffd46c7b18c6bc.png)\n\nConsider the arc of the curve $y=2x-{x}^{2}$ that lies in the first quadrant between its $x$-intercepts. What integral gives the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis?",
      "worked_solution": "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi y\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $y=f(x),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we find where the curve intersects the $x$-axis by solving the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ x(2-x) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=0$ to $x=2.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-{x}^{2})=2-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x-{x}^{2})\\sqrt{1+{(2-2x)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x-{x}^{2})\\sqrt{5-8x+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-126540-a",
